$DATUM 2.2 Baylis-Hillman reaction involving acrylamide and various aldehydes
Procedure using condition set A: A 1 mL reaction vessel equipped with a
stirring bar was charged with acrylamide (142 mg, 2.0 mmol), DABCO (224
mg, 2.0 mmol) and phenol (47 mg, 0.5 mmol). Note: If the aldehyde
component is a solid it is added at this stage. The vessel was fitted
with a septum, gently flushed with Ar gas and fitted with an Ar balloon.
A tBuOH/H2O solvent mixture (120 μL) and the aldehyde (3.0 mmol) were
then added via syringe. The resulting homogeneous mixture was stirred at
55 °C for the time indicated in Table 3 and allowed to cool. Column
chromatography of the reaction mixture (95:5 CH2Cl2/MeOH) yielded the
required Baylis-Hillman adducts.
2-[Hydroxy(2-nitrophenyl)methyl]acrylamide (13), yield 91% Spectral data
consistent with that reported in the literature2 M.p. 136-138 °C; IR
(film) 3446, 3215, 2925, 1666, 1523 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
5.48 (s, 1H), 5.89 (s, 1H), 5.94 (d, 1H, J= 5.5 Hz), 6.05 (d, 1H, J= 5.5
Hz), 7.02 (s, 1H), 7.48 (t, 1H, J= 7.5 Hz), 7.57 (m, 2H), 7.65 (t, 1H, J=
7.5 Hz), 7.84 (d, 1H, J= 8.0 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 65.7,
118.3, 123.8, 128.3, 128.9, 132.8, 137.3, 146.2, 148.5, 168.1; HRMS (EI)
m/z (MH+) calcd for C10H11N2O4 223.0719, found 223.0712; Anal. Calcd for
C10H10N2O4 C, 54.05; H, 4.54; N, 12.61. Found C, 53.85; H, 4.50; N,
12.37.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acrylamide in the Baylis-Hillman Reaction: Expanded reaction scope and
the unexpected superiority of DABCO over more basic tertiary amine
catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
