$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (6E)-(2S,4R,5R)-8-Ethoxycarbonyloxy-2-benzyloxy-4,6-dimethyl-5-hydroxy-6-octen-3-one
(74). To a -78 °C solution of cHex2BCl (11.0 mL, 50.4 mmol) in Et2O (60
mL) was added Et3N (8.1 mL, 58.1 mmol), followed by a solution of 728
(7.4 g, 38.7 mmol) in Et2O (2 x 20 ml). The reaction was stirred at -78
°C for 1 h then at 0 °C for 1 h. After cooling to -78 °C, a solution of
734 (8.7 g, 50.4 mmol) in Et2O (10 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred
for 1 h at -78 °C and placed in the freezer for 3 d. The reaction mixture
was partitioned between Et2O and a 1.0 M aqueous NaH2PO4/NaOH buffer (pH
~ 7), the organic extract was concentrated to give an oil which was taken
up in MeOH (100 mL) and 1.0 M aqueous NaH2PO4/NaOH buffer (pH ~ 7) (100
mL) was added and the solution was stirred at 0 °C. H2O2 (100 mL, 30%
solution in H2O) was added dropwise. After stirring at room temperature
for 2 h, the mixture was diluted with H2O and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3×).
The combined organic layers were washed with saturated aqueous Na2CO3,
brine, dried over MgSO4, and the solvent and cyclohexanol were evaporated
under reduce pressure and heating (~80 °C) to give the crude product
which was purified by flash chromatography using 40% Et2O/hexane to yield
74 (12.1 g, 86%) as a colourless liquid. Rf = 0.34 (30% hexanes:ether);
(6E)-(2S,4R,5R)-8-Ethoxycarbonyloxy-2-benzyloxy-4,6-dimethyl-5-hydroxy-6-octen-3-one
(74). , yield 12.1 g, 86% 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.37-7.26 (5H, m),
5.75 (1H, tt, J = 6.9, 1.4 Hz), 4.69 (2H, d, J = 7.1 Hz), 4.55 (2H, s),
3.19 (1H, dq, J = 7.1, 3.0 Hz), 2.95 (1H, d, J = 2.5 Hz), 1.61 (3H, s),
1.38 (3H, d, J = 6.9 Hz), 1.30 (3H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.03 (3H, d, J = 7.1
Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 215.7, 155.0, 140.2, 137.3, 128.3, 127.8,
127.6, 119.4, 79.3, 74.0, 71.5, 63.7, 43.1, 16.7, 14.1, 13.4, 9.9; IR
(film) ν 3513, 2983, 2936, 2875, 1743, 1586, 1452, 1369, 1253, 1114 cm-1;
HRMS (EI): m/z calcd. for ([M-OH]+) = 347.1874, found = 347.1858; [α]20D
-20 (c 3.1, CHCl3).
