$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-[2-(3-Cyclohex-1-enyl-1-hydroxyprop-2-ynyl)-phenyl]-3-trimethylsilylprop-2-yn-1-ol
14 n-BuLi (4.62 mL, 1.6 M in hexanes) was slowly added to a solution of
trimethylsylilacetylene (0.76 g, 7.75 mmol) in dry THF (10 mL) cooled at
-78 °C, and the mixture was stirred for 5 minutes before adding to a
cooled solution of phthaldehyde 4 (0.95 g, 7.05 mmol) in THF (10 mL).
After 10 minutes a solution of the lithium acetylide of
ethynylcyclohexene [prepared by reacting n-BuLi (4.84 mL, 1.6 M in
hexanes) with ethynylcyclohexene (0.90 g, 8.45 mmol)] was added via
canula and the reaction mixture was allowed to reach room temperature and
stirred for 60 minutes. The reaction was quenched with a saturated aquous
solution of NH4Cl, diluted with EtOAc and washed with brine (3 x 25 mL).
The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and evaporated to
dryness. The crude residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane/EtOAc 4:1 as eluent to yield 14 (2.25 g, 94%) as
a colorless oil. NMR spectra show a mixture of isomers; for 1H NMR only
the signals of the mayor isomer are given; for 13C NMR all the observed
peaks are given (some of them are duplicated due to the presence of
isomers). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ: 7.87-7.60 (m, 2H, ArH), 7.44-7.33 (m, 2H,
ArH), 6.24-5.87 (m, 3H, 2 x ArCH + C=CH), 3.44 (broad s, 1H, OH), 3.10
(broad s, 1H, OH), 2.22-2.03 (m, 4H, CH 2), 1.71-1.52 (m, 4H, CH 2), 0.22
(s, 9H, Si(CH 3)3); 13C NMR/DEPT (CDCl3) δ: 138.5 (C), 138.0 (C), 138.0
(C), 137.5 (C), 137.5 (C), 135.7 (CH), 135.6 (CH), 129.0 (CH), 128.9
(CH), 128.8 (CH), 128.8 (CH), 127.9 (CH), 119.9 (C), 119.8 (C), 104.4
(C), 104.1 (C), 92.3 (C), 92.2 (C), 89.3 (C), 88.9 (C), 85.1 (C), 84.9
(C), 63.5 (CH), 63.3 (CH), 62.6 (CH), 61.9 (CH), 28.9 (CH2), 28.8 (CH2),
25.5 (CH2), 22.1 (CH2), 21.3 (CH2), -0.3 (Si(CH3)3); MS (70 eV) m/z (%):
338 (M+, 47), 337 (100), 336 (60), 335 (83), 329 (63), 327 (64) ... 73
(48).
