$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2. General procedure for the synthesis
homoallyl alchoals: A mixture of 1-bromo-2-propene (3 mmol) or
1-bromo-2-methyl-2-propene (3 mmol), indium metal (1.2 mmol) and sodium
iodide (3 mmol) in dimethylformamide (3-4 mL) was stirred at rt until the
complex was completely formed. A solution of bromoaldehyde in
dimethylformamide was then added to the reaction mixture. The reaction
was monitered by TLC change and after 5-6h the reaction mixture was
quenched with a few drops of 1N HCl solution. It was then extracted with
dichloromethane which was thoroughly washed with sodium thiosulphate and
then brine water. Evaporation of the solvent followed by purification by
silica gel (60-120 mesh) column chromatography provided the pure product.
Compound (2g), yellow liquid, yield 82%, 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400MHz) δ: 2.10
(d, 1H, J= 3.2Hz), 2.53-2.61 (m, 1H), 2.71-2.85 (m, 5H), 5.10-5.18 (m,
2H), 5.26 (m, 1H), 5.82- 5.92 (m, 1H) 7.11-7.22(m, 3H), 7.88(d, 1H, J=
7.6Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3 ,100MHz) δ: 29.66, 36.11, 39.57, 74.00 , 117.78,
124.75, 125.94, 126.21, 127.12, 127.50, 132.36, 134.57, 135.65, 135.81.
