$DATUM (E)-7-(tert-Butyldimethylsiloxy)-2-methyl-9-phenyl-4-(toluene-4-sulfonyl)non-4-en-3-ol
2a To a solution of 270 mg (610 μmol, 1.0 equiv) of vinyl sulfone 1'a in
7 mL of THF at -78°C was added dropwise, over 10 min, 920 μL (670 μmol,
1.1 equiv) of a 0.73 M solution of PhLi.LiBr in ether. The resulting
solution was stirred at -78°C for 20 min and 66 μL (730 μmol, 1.2 equiv)
of freshly distilled isobutyraldehyde was then added. The reaction
mixture was stirred at -78°C for 30 min, quenched with 10 mL of a
saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution and diluted with 100 mL of ethyl
acetate. The layers were separated and the organic layer was washed with
brine, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The crude
residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(ether/petroleum ether 10:90, 15:85, 20:80) to afford 226 mg (72%) of a
1:1 mixture of the 2 diastereomers of 2a as a colorless oil.
(E)-7-(tert-Butyldimethylsiloxy)-2-methyl-9-phenyl-4-(toluene-4-sulfonyl)non-4-en-3-ol
2a, yield 226 mg (72%) 1H NMR(400MHz, CDCl3): I 7.76-7.74 (m, 2H),
7.30-7.12 (m, 7H), 6.99 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 0.5H), 6.97 (t, J = 7.0 Hz,
0.5H), 4.17 (dd, J = 9.1, 7.0 Hz, 0.5H), 4.10 (dd, J = 9.4, 7.9 Hz,
0.5H), 3.91- 3.84 (m, 1H), 2.78 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 0.5H), 2.75 (d, J = 7.9
Hz, 0.5H), 2.69-2.44 (m, 4H), 2.42 (s, 1.5H), 2.41 (s, 1.5H), 2.13-1.97
(m, 1H), 1.78-1.68 (m, 2H), 1.03 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1.5H), 1.00 (d, J = 6.8
Hz, 1.5H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.64 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1.5H), 0.62 (d, J = 6.8 Hz,
1.5H), 0.06 (s, 3H), 0.05 (s, 1.5H), 0.04 (s, 1.5H). 13C NMR(100MHz,
CDCl3): I 144.9, 144.6, 144.3, 141.9, 141.7, 138.1, 138.1, 129.9, 128.5,
128.4, 128.1, 126.0, 75.3, 75.0, 70.5, 39.2, 39.0, 36.0, 35.9, 33.5,
33.5, 31.7, 31.5, 25.9, 21.7, 19.5, 19.2, 19.2, 19.1, 18.1, -4.4, -4.4.
IR (film): 3516 (br), 3084, 3062, 3026, 2955, 2856, 1635, 1598, 1495,
1470, 1404, 1386, 1363, 1300, 1255, 1144, 1084, 1033 cm-1. MS (DI, CI
NH3): m/z 534 (M+NH4 +), 517 (M+H+). Anal. Calcd for C29H44O4SSi: C,
67.40; H, 8.58. Found: C, 67.41; H, 8.61.
