$DATUM 1-(5-Bromo-2-thienyl)-2,2,2-trifluoroethanol (4). A solution of
5-bromothiophene-2-carboxaldehyde 3 (1.0 g, 5.3 mmol) and CsF (80 mg,
0.53 mmol) in DME (20 mL) was treated with TMSCF3 (0.92 mL, 6.3 mmol) and
then stirred for 2 h at RT. The reaction mixture was quenched by adding
3N HCl and stirred for 30 min. The mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2, and
the organic phase was separated, washed with brine, and dried.
Evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure gave a crude, which was
purified by silica gel chromatography (1-10% EtOAc/petroleum ether
gradient) to give 4 (1.3 g, 95%) as an oil. 1H NMR(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.00
(d, J = 3.7 Hz, 1H), 6.95 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (q, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H),
3.62 (br s, 1H). MS (ES) C6H4F3BrOS requires 260, 262; found 243, 245
(M-OH) + .
