$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for LDA-Mediated Addition
Reaction of Vinydienecyclopropanes 1 with Aldehyde 3. Under an argon
atmosphere, to a solution of vinylidenecyclopropane 1 (0.2 mmol) in THF
(2.0 mL) was added LDA (0.4 mmol) at -78 °C , the resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at -78 °C for about 2 h, Then aldehyde 3 (0.3 mmol)
was added and the reaction solution was further stirred for 2 h at the
same reaction temperature. Then the reaction mixture was quenched by the
addition of the solution of ammonium chloride and warmed to room
temperature. The reaction solution was diluted with ether (10.0 mL *3).
The organic layers were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure and the residue was purified by a flash
column chromatography. 4d, A pale yellow solid. Mp: 136-137 °C. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 300 MHz, TMS) δ 2.06 (d, 1H, J = 2.4 Hz, OH), 2,17 (s, 3H, CH3),
2.40 (s, 3H, CH3), 6.24 (d, 1H, J = 2.4 Hz), 6.54 (s, 1H), 7.04-7.25 (m,
18H, Ar), 7.37 (d, 2H, J = 7.8 Hz, Ar), 7.56 (s, 1H, Ar), 7.70 (s, 1H,
Ar), 7.82 (d, 1H, J = 8.7 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz, TMS) δ 21.2, 21.7,
50.2, 73.2, 125.98, 126.02, 126.2, 126.4, 126.6, 126.9, 127.3, 127.4,
128.2, 128.26, 128.31, 128.8, 129.0, 130.0, 130.5, 133.2, 134.6, 135.0,
136.8, 137.9, 139.8, 140.0, 142.1, 142.9, 143.6. IR (CH2Cl2) ν 3567,
3439, 3059, 3025, 2920, 2361, 2343, 1599, 1507, 1494, 1452, 1360, 1265,
1181, 1032, 826, 737, 700 cm-1. MS (%) (EI) m/z 486 (M+-17, 100), 317
(71), 302 (44), 487 (41), 425 (38), 188 (37.4), 254 (36.5), 408 (34).
HRMS (EI) calcd. for C38H32O: 504.2453, Found: 504.2453.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM LDA-Mediated Selective Addition Reaction of Vinylidenecyclopropanes with
Aldehydes, Ketones, and Enones: Facile Synthesis of Vinylcyclopropenes,
Allenols, and 1,3-Enynes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lu, Jian-Mei; Shi, Min
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(10), 1943-1946

