$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Reaction Procedure for the
Morita-Baylis-Hillman Reactions. To a mixture of arylaldehyde (0.15
mmol), DABCO (0.03 mmol) and catalyst 2h (0.03 mmol) in solvent were
added 2-cycohexen-1-one or 2-cyclopenten-1-one (0.45 mmol) under argon
atmosphere and the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for
the required time indicated in the Tables. After the reaction solution
was concentrated under reduced pressure, the residue was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (Eluent: EtOAc/petroleum ether = 1/4)
to afford the pure product 5. 2-(Hydroxy-p-tolylmethyl)cyclohex-2-enone.
[α]20D = +5.00 (c 1.10, CHCl3).1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz, TMS): δ 1.95-2.03
(2H, m, CH2), 2.33 (3H, s, CH3), 2.36-2.47 (4H, m, CH2), 3.40 (1H, s,
OH), 5.52 (1H, s, CH), 6.75 (1H, t, J = 3.9 Hz, CH), 7.15 (2H, d, J = 8.1
Hz, Ar), 7.24 (2H, d, J = 8.1 Hz, Ar).13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 21.1,
22.5, 25.7, 38.5, 72.4, 126.3, 129.0, 137.1, 138.6, 141.0, 147.2, 200.5.
Enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC with a Chiralcel AS-H column
hexane/iPrOH = 85/15, 0.7 mL/min, 230 nm, tminor = 15.63 min, tmajor =
19.46 min; 76% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, 76% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Morita-Baylis-Hillman Reaction of Arylaldehydes with
2-Cyclohexen-1-one Catalyzed by Chiral Bis(Thio)urea and DABCO
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shi, Min; Liu, Xu-Guang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(6), 1043-1046

