$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: β-Hydroxy oxoester (4). MgI2 (0.167 g, 0.6
mmol) was added to a stirred solution of O- benzylacetate (3) (0.075 g,
0.5 mmol) and benzaldehyde (61 μL, 0.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.5 mL), followed
by the addition of i-Pr2NEt (0.11 mL, 0.65 mmol). Stirring was continued
for 20 h and EtOAc (2.5 mL) and 10% (v/v) aqueous HCl (2.5 mL) were
added. Stirring was continued for 15 min and the mixture was partitioned
between EtOAc (15 mL) and H2O (2 mL). The aqueous phase was extracted
with EtOAc (3 x 5mL) and the combined organic extracts were washed with
saturated aqueous NaCl, dried (MgSO4), and evaporated. Flash
chromatography over silica gel, using 10:90 EtOAc hexanes gave 4 as a
pure, colorless oil. β-Hydroxy thioester (14). Flash chromatography over
silica gel, using 10:90 EtOAc-hexanes gave 14, yield 96% as a pure,
light-yellow oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ 7.41-7.23 (m, 6H), 6.33-6.18
(m, 2H), 5.20 (X of an ABX system, broad apparent td, (J = 2.7, 8.7 Hz, 1
H) 4.20 and 4.17 (AB q, ΔνAB = 10.4 Hz, J = 15.3 Hz,2H), 3.09-2.88 [m,
3H, including A of an ABX system, apparent dd, at δ 3.03 (J = 8.8,15.8
Hz), B of an ABX system, apparent dd, at δ 2.93 (J = 3.9, 15.8 Hz),
overlapping abroad d at δ 2.92 (J = 2.4 Hz)]; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ
197.5, 150.1, 142.4,142.3, 128.7, 128.0, 125.7, 110.7, 108.2, 70.8, 52.4,
25.8; ESI-MS m/z calcd for C14H14NaO3S: 285.1, found: 284.8
