$DATUM Ethyl-2-(hydroxy-(4-nitrophenyl)-methyl)-but-3-enoate (13). The product
was purified by silica gel chromatography using pentane-ethyl acetate
(4:1) as eluent giving a mixture of diastereomers, a All reactions were
conducted in THF in the presence of (SnMe3)2 using 5 mol % Pd catalyst.
Method A: [η 3-allyl)PdCl]2. Yield 88% Diastereomer A: 1H NMR: δ 8.14 (m,
2H), 7.46-7.52 (m, 2H), 5.87 (ddd, 17.4 Hz, 10.2 Hz, 9.0 Hz, 1H), 5.23
(dd, 10.2 Hz, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 5.16 (dd, 5.0 Hz, 2.5 Hz, 1H), 5.07 (dt, 17.4
Hz, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (q, 7.1 Hz, 2H), 3.46 (d, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 3.28 (dd,
9.0 Hz, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 1.17 (t, 7.1 Hz, 3H). Diastereomer B: 1H NMR: δ 8.14
(m, 2H), 7.46-7.52 (m, 2H), 5.70 (ddd, 17.2 Hz, 10.3 Hz, 8.9 Hz, 1H),
5.12 (d, 10.3 Hz, 1H), 4.99-5.05 (m, 2H), 4.15 (q, 7.1 Hz, 2H), 3.50 (d,
5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.36 (dd, 8.5 Hz, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 1.21 (t, 7.1 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR
for diastereomers A and B: δ 172.7, 148.8, 148.3, 147.8, 147.7, 131.7,
130.7, 127.8, 127.6, 123.7 (2 C), 121.7, 120.7, 74.5, 73.1, 61.7, 58.0,
57.8, 14.3, 14.3. MS (EI): m/z (rel intens) 265 (M+, 2), 248 (6), 152
(18), 114 (46), 86 (100).
