$DATUM 60-29-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Scale-up Reaction of 2-Methylfuran with n-Butyl glyoxylate with 0.1% of
the Catalyst (Conditions E): The reaction of 2-methylfuran (10 mmol) with
n-butyl glyoxylate (12 mmol) was carried out using 0.1 mol% of catalyst,
generated from 6,6′-Br2BINOL (9.3 mg, 0.021 mmol) and Ti(OPri)4 (2.95 μL,
2.85 mg, 0.010 mmol) in 0.4 mL of toluene for 2h at room temperature, and
then diluted with 1.6 mL of toluene. Next the reaction was curried out
according general scale-up procedure using conditions E: 24 h at 20°C.
The yield of the product 3a was 92% (92% ee).
(R)-(5-Methyl-furan-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (3a), yield 92%
oil 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.25-6.24 (m, 1H), 5.94-5.93 (m, 1H),
5.11 (s, 1H), 4.29-4.18 (m, 2H), 3.32 (s, 1H), 2.27 (s, 3H), 1.65-1.58
(m, 2H), 1.36-1.26 (m, 2H), 0.89 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100
MHz, CHCl3) δ = 171.8 (C), 152.8 (C), 149.0 (C), 109.6 (CH), 106.4 (CH),
66.9 (CH), 66.2 (CH2), 30.4 (CH2), 18.8 (CH2), 13.51 (CH3), 13.49 (CH3)
ppm; IR (CHCl3) 3483, 3132, 3109, 2935, 2875, 1741, 1562, 1384, 1273,
