$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedures: General Procedure for the Reaction of Furans with n-Butyl
glyoxylate (Conditions A, B and C): In a 5 mL round-bottomed flask closed
with a septum, 6,6′-Br2BINOL (conditions A: 18.7 mg, 0.042 mmol; B and C:
46.75 mg, 0.105 mmol) was dissolved in toluene (A: 0.8 mL; B and C: 2.0
mL). To a stirred solution of the ligand, titanium tetraisopropoxide (A:
5.9 μL, 5.7 mg, 0.020 mmol, 2.0 mol%; B and C: 14.75 μL, 14.25 mg, 0.050
mmol, 5.0 mol%) was added via syringe directly under the solution surface
at room temperature (inert atmosphere was not required). The resulting
dark red mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature (in conditions A
the catalyst solution was diluted with 3.2 mL of toluene) and cooled to
0°C. Then n-butyl glyoxylate (0.195 g, 1.5 mmol) was introduced and,
finally, after 5-10 min, the corresponding furan (1.0 mmol) was added at
0°C and stirred at temperature and for time reported in Table 3 (A: 2-3h
at 0°C; B: 20h at 20°C; C: 4h at 0°C). The reaction mixture did not
require any work-up and was directly subjected to flash chromatography
using hexane followed by hexane/AcOEt (9:1) as an eluent. The yields of
products from substituted furans (1a, 1c-m) were 76-98% (88-97% ee).
(R)-(5-Methyl-furan-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (3a): oil 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.25-6.24 (m, 1H), 5.94-5.93 (m, 1H), 5.11 (s, 1H),
4.29-4.18 (m, 2H), 3.32 (s, 1H), 2.27 (s, 3H), 1.65-1.58 (m, 2H),
1.36-1.26 (m, 2H), 0.89 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CHCl3)
δ = 171.8 (C), 152.8 (C), 149.0 (C), 109.6 (CH), 106.4 (CH), 66.9 (CH),
66.2 (CH2), 30.4 (CH2), 18.8 (CH2), 13.51 (CH3), 13.49 (CH3) ppm; IR
(CHCl3) 3483, 3132, 3109, 2935, 2875, 1741, 1562, 1384, 1273, 1219, 1074,
1021, 788 cm-1; HPLC analysis: 97% ee (OD-H, 5% i-PrOH in hexane, 1.0
mL/min, λ = 205 nm, tR = 7.5 min, minor, tR = 9.4 min, major); [α]D20 =
-47.7 (c = 1.2, CHCl3); HRMS (ESI) calcd. for C11H16O4Na [(M+Na)+]:
235.09408; found: 235.09519.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
