$DATUM General Procedure for Scale-up Reaction of Furans with n-Butyl glyoxylate
(0.5 mol% of the Catalyst; Conditions D and E): To a solution of
6,6′-Br2BINOL (46.75 mg, 0.105 mmol) in toluene (2.0 mL) in a 10 mL
flask, titanium tetraisopropoxide (14.75 μL, 14.25 mg, 0.050 mmol, 0.5
mol%) was added via syringe directly under the solution surface at room
temperature (inert atmosphere was not required). The resulting dark red
mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature and cooled to 0°C. Then
n-butyl glyoxylate (1.562 g, 12 mmol) was introduced and, finally, after
10 min, the corresponding furan (10 mmol) was added at 0°C and stirred at
temperature and time reported in Scheme 3 (conditions D: 5 h at 0°C; E:
24 h at 20°C). The reaction mixture was directly subjected to flash
chromatography using hexane followed by hexane/AcOEt (9:1) as an eluent.
The yields of the products were 90-95% (91-95% ee).
(R)-(5-Methyl-furan-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (3a): oil 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.25-6.24 (m, 1H), 5.94-5.93 (m, 1H), 5.11 (s, 1H),
4.29-4.18 (m, 2H), 3.32 (s, 1H), 2.27 (s, 3H), 1.65-1.58 (m, 2H),
