$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A for synthesis of
phenoxypropargyl alcohols:1 At -78 °C, n-BuLi (1.6 M in n-hexane; 2.70
mL, 4.30 mmol) was added to a solution of 1,2-dichlorovinyl phenyl ether
(400 mg, 2.1 mmol) in Et2O (4.4 mL), and the reaction mixture was allowed
to warm to -20 °C over 2 h, thus forming lithiumphenoxyacetylide. After
cooling to-78 °C again, the carbonyl compound (0.88 mmol) was added. The
reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred
until the complete consumption of starting compounds. The reaction
mixture was quenched with sat. aq. NH4Cl and then extracted with EtOAc.
The combined organic layer was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and
evaporated. The residue was purified by column chromatography (silica
gel, n-hexane/EtOAc). The phenoxypropargyl alcohols 5a-8r.
3-phenoxy-1-phenylprop-2-yn-1ol (5a): 1.69 g of 5a was obtained from 1 g
(9.43 mmol) of benzaldehyde from general procedure A.
3-phenoxy-1-(thiophen-2-yl)prop-2-yn-1-ol (5j):1.80 g of 5j was obtained
from 1 g (9.00 mmol) of thiophene-2-aldehyde from general procedure A.
Yield 87%; orange gum. Rf = 0.55 (SiO2, 20% EtOAc/hexanes);1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.43-7.34 (m, 2H), 7.33-7.26 (m, 3H), 7.23-7.12 (m, 2H),
7.03-6.95 (m, 1H), 5.85 (d, J = 5.19 Hz, 1H), 2.49 (d, J = 5.93 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 155.8, 145.8, 129.9, 126.9, 125.9, 125.4,
124.8, 115.1, 88.8, 60.3, 45.0; IR (neat) ν 3428, 3019, 2273, 1632, 1488,
1385, 1215, 1142, 1024, 757, 626 cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calcd for C13H11O2S
[M +H]+ 231.0480, found 231.0481.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
