$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure: A flame-dried flask was
charged with Ni(COD)2 (10 mol%, stored and weighed in an inert atmosphere
glove box) and 8.0 mL of THF. The acrylate (1.0 equiv), aldehyde (1.5
equiv), and iodobenzene (0.2-1.0 equiv) were sequentially added by
syringe, followed by addition of triethylborane (2.0 equiv), and the
mixture was heated at 72º C for 6-8 h. The reaction mixture was quenched
with 1.0 M NaOH, extracted with 3 x 15 mL ethyl acetate, washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated. The crude residue was
chromatographed using 5% ethyl acetate/hexanes to 20% ethyl
acetate/hexanes to afford the product. The yields reported are for a
mixture of inseparable diastereomers and are isolated yields taken as an
average of at least two runs. Diastereomeric ratios were determined by
1H-NMR or GCMS. In addition to comparisons to known compounds and
characterization of six-membered acetonides, analysis of J values was
also useful in confirming stereochemistry. syn aldol products typically
display J values of 3-6 Hz between the two chiral centers whereas anti
aldol products display J values of 5-9 Hz.1
2-Methyl-3-hydroxy-3-phenylpropionic acid t-butyl ester (2)
2-Methyl-3-furan-2-yl-3-hydroxypropionic acid t-butyl ester (Table 3
Entry 3) Following the general procedure, iodobenzene (112 µL, 1.0 mmol),
2-furaldehyde (166 µL, 2.0 mmol), tert-butyl acrylate (146 µL, 1.0 mmol),
triethylborane (2.0 mL, 1.0 M solution in THF, 2.0 mmol), and Ni(COD)2
(28 mg, 0.1 mmol) were used to obtain the title compound as a mixture of
diastereomers, after flash chromatography, 206 mg (91%, dr 88:12) as a
colorless oil. 1H NMR assignments for the major (syn) diastereomer: (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.35 (m, 1H), 6.33 (dd, J = 2.0, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 6.27 (dt, J =
3.2, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 4.94 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 3.08 (bs, 1H), 2.87 (dq, J =
5.2, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 1.42 (s, 9H), 1.18 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) 174.3, 154.4, 141.8, 110.1, 106.7, 81.3, 69.0, 44.8, 27.9,
12.0; IR (film) 3428, 2977, 1724, 1504, 1457, 1368 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd
for C12H18O4 226.1205, found: (M)+ 226.1206. Diagnostic 1H NMR signals
for the minor (anti) diastereomer include the following: δ 4.72 (d, J =
7.2 Hz, 1H), 1.45 (s, 9H), 1.11 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, dr: 88:12
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Surprising Role of Aryl Halides in Nickel-Catalyzed Reductive Aldol
Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chrovian, Christa C.; Montgomery, John
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(3), 537-540

