$DATUM (E)-1-[(4R,6S)-6-Allyl-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-4-yl]-4-hydroxy-6-phenylhex-5-en-2-one
(29): NEt3 (170 μL, 121 mg, 1.19 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was added to a solution
of 24 (230 mg, 1.08 mmol) in Et2O (10 mL) at room temp. The reaction
mixture was cooled to -78°C and nBu2BOTf (250 μL, 312 mg, 1.14 mmol, 1.05
equiv) was added dropwise. The resulting white heterogeneous mixture was
stirred for 30 min at -78°C followed by the slowly addition of
cinnamaldehyde (26) (150 μL, 158 mg, 1.19 mmol, 1.1 equiv) dissolved in
Et2O (1.5 mL) over a period of 10 min. After 2 h at -78°C the reaction
mixture was quenched cautiously with a pH 7 buffer/MeOH [7 mL, 1:6 (v:v)]
solution and warmed to 0°C followed by the addition of a 30% H2O2/MeOH [3
mL, 1:2 (v:v)] solution. After 30 min at 0°C the reaction m ixture was
warmed to room temp. and stirred for an additional 1 h. The solution was
diluted with Et2O (5 mL) and H2O (5 mL) and the phases were separated.
The aq. phase was extracted with Et2O (3 x 5 mL) and the combined organic
phases were washed with satd. aq. NaHCO3 (5 mL), brine (5 mL) and dried
over MgSO4. After removal of the solvent under reduced pressure, flash
chromatography on silicagel [c-C6H12/EtOAc 4:1 (v:v)] provided the title
compound. Colorless oil, yield 373 mg, 70%. [α]20589 = +16.3, [α]20578 =
+17.3, [α]20546 = +19.8, [α]20436 = +33.2 (c = 0.88, CHCl3). 1H NMR
(250.1 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.25 and 1.28 [2 x s, 6 H, 2'-(CH3)2], AB signal
(δA = 1.52, δB = 1.64, JAB = 12.8 Hz, A part additionally split by JA,4'
= 9.6 Hz, JA,6 ' = 6.4 Hz, B part additionally split by JB,6 ' = 9.0 Hz,
JB,4' = 6.1 Hz, 2 H, 5'-H2), AB signal (δA = 2.12, δB = 2.24, JAB = 14.3
Hz, A part additionally split by JA,2" = 7.0 Hz, JA,6 ' = 6.3 Hz,
4JA,3''-H(trans) = 4JA,3''-H(cis) = 1.1 Hz, B part additionally split by
JB,2" = JB,6 ' = 6.5 Hz, 4JB,3''-H(trans) = 4JB,3''-H(cis) = 1.3 Hz, 2 H,
1''-H2), AB signal (δA = 2.41, δB = 2.67, JAB = 15.9 Hz, A part
additionally split by JA,4' = 4.5 Hz, B part additionally split by JB,4'
= 8.5 Hz, 2 H, 1-H2), AB signal (δA = 2.65, δB = 2.73, JAB = 17.1 Hz, A
part additionally split by JA,4 = 7.7 Hz, B part additionally split by
JB,4 = 4.5 Hz, 2 H, 3-H2), 3.09 (br. d, 1 H, J4-OH,4 = 3.2 Hz, 4-OH),
3.79 (dddd, 1 H, J6',5'-H(B) = 9.1 Hz, J6',5'-H(A) = J6',1''-H(A) =
J6',1"-H(B) = 6.5 Hz, 6'-H), 4.24 (dddd, 1 H, J4',5'-H(A) = 9.4 Hz,
J4',1-H(B) = 8.5 Hz, J4',5'-H(B) = 5.9 Hz, J4',1-H(A) = 4.6 Hz, 4'-H),
4.70 (mc, 1 H, 4-H), 4.98 [dddd, 1 H, J3''-H(cis),2'' = 10.2 Hz,
2J3''-(cis),3''-H(trans) = 2.1 Hz, 4J3''-H(cis),1''-H(A) =
4J3''-H(cis),1''-H(B) = 1.2 Hz, 3''-H(cis)], 5.02 [dddd, 1 H,
J3''-H(trans),2'' = 17.1 Hz, 2J3''-H(trans),3''-H(cis) = 1.9 Hz,
4J3''-H(trans),1''-H(A) = 4J3''-H(trans),1''-H(B) = 1.3 Hz,
3''-H(trans)], 5.71 (dddd, 1 H, J2'',3''-H(trans) = 17.1 Hz,
J2'',3''-H(cis) = 10.3 Hz, J2'',1''-H(A) = J2'',1''-H(B) = 6.8 Hz,
2''-H), 6.13 (dd, 1 H, J5,6 = 15.9 Hz, J5,4 = 6.0 Hz, 5-H), 6.57 (dd, 1
H, J6,5 = 15.9 Hz, 4J6,4 = 15.9 Hz, 6-H), 7.14-7.32 ppm (m, 5 H, 2 x
ortho-H, 2 x meta-H, para-H). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 24.72 and
24.84 [2'-(CH3)2], 37.51 (C-5'), 40.10 (C-1''), 49.32 (C-1), 50.43 (C-3),
63.33 (C-4), 66.15 (C-4'), 68.47 (C-6'), 100.73 (C-2'), 117.19 (C-3''),
126.55 and 126.57 (2 x ortho-C), 127.82 (para-C), 128.64 and 128.66 (2 x
meta-C), 130.20 (C-6), 130.43 (C-5), 134.25 (C-2''), 136.60 (ipso-C),
209.09 ppm (C-2). IR (film): ν = 3400, 3080, 3025, 2985, 2935, 1710,
1645, 1495, 1450, 1380, 1225, 1175, 1115, 1070, 970, 945, 915, 750, 695
cm-1. HRMS (pos. ESI, MeOH): C21H28O4Na (M+H)+ calc. 367.1885 found
376.1882 (Δ = -0.9 ppm).
