4-[(5R,2E)-1-Oxo-7-phenyl-5-hydroxy-2,6-heptadienyl]morpholine (51)
(Table 7, entry 3) Diisopropylethylamine (9 µL, 0.05 mmol, 0.2 equiv) was
added via syringe to a flamedried, 20-mL, Schlenk flask under Ar
containing a solution of 4 mg (0.005 mmol, 0.02 equiv) of
bisphosphoramide (R,R)-3 in CH2Cl2 (2.5 mL). To this solution was added
32 µL (0.25 mmol, 1.0 equiv) of cinnamaldehyde in one portion and the
reaction mixture was cooled to -78 °C (bath temperature) over 15 min. To
the resulting solution was added 32 µL (0.275 mmol, 1.1 equiv) of SiCl4
in one portion. Then, 81 mg (0.3 mmol, 1.2 equiv) of 45 was added
dropwise over 2 min via syringe. The resulting mixture was stirred at -78
°C for 2 h whereupon 3.0 mL of chilled CH2Cl2 was added before the cold
reaction mixture was poured into a rapidly stirring solution of 1/1 sat.
aq. NaHCO3/ sat. aq. KF (25 mL) at 0 °C. This biphasic mixture was
stirred vigorously for 2 h after which the organic layer was removed and
the aqueous layer was washed with CH2Cl2 (3 x 30 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4 (5 g), filtered and the filtrate
was concentrated in vacuo. The ratio of
γ-1,2-51/α-1,2-51/γ-1,4-51/α-1,4-51 was determined to be 97/0/1/2 by 1H
NMR (500 MHz) analysis of the crude reaction mixture. The residue was
purified by column chromatography (SiO2 (12 g), 2 cm diam., EtOAc (100
mL) to EtOAc/MeOH, 19/1 (100 mL)) to yield 70 mg (97%) of γ-1,2-51 as a
white solid. Data for γ-1,2-51: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.38 (d, J =
8.4, 2 H, HC(9)), 7.32 (dt, J = 7.7, 1.7, 2 H, HC(10)) 7.25 (tt, J = 7.5,
1.3, 1 H, HC(11)), 6.92 (dt, J = 15.1, 7.3, 1 H, HC(3)), 6.61 (d, J =
15.9, 1 H, HC(7)), 6.32 (dt, J = 15.1, 1.5, 1 H, HC(2)), 6.24 (dd, J =
15.9, 6.3, 1 H, HC(6)), 4.48 (dq, J = 6.6, 1.2, 1 H, HC(5)), 3.65 (m, 8
H, H2C(12,13)), 2.58-2.54 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 2.09 (br s, 1 H, OH) TLC: Rf
0.14 (EtOAc) [UV(254 nm)] SFC: (R)-γ-1,2-51, t R 2.40 min (95.6%);
(S)-γ-1,2-51, t R 4.15 min (4.4%) (Chiralpak OB, 125 psi, 40 ºC, 20.0%
MeOH in CO2, 3.0 mL/min, 220 nm)
