$DATUM 1-(6-hydoxy-2-iodo-3,3-methylcyclohex-1-enyl)-3-methylbut-2-en-1-one:
Tetra-n-butylammonium iodide (922 mg, 2.50 mmol) was added to a stirred
solution of aldehyde 1a (369 mg, 1.92 mmol) in 21 mL of dry
dichloromethane at -78 °C. TiCl4 (1 M in Dichloromethane, 2.5 mL, 2.5
mmol) was then added dropwise. After 1 h, the mixture was warmed to 0 °C
for 1 h. The mixture was diluted with 10 mL of ethyl acetate, quenched
with 5 mL of saturated NaHCO3 solution, and extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 x 40 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with saturated
Na2S2O3 solution, brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated. The
resulting residue was purified by flash chromatography (hexanes:ethyl
acetate, 80:20) to give cyclohexenyl alcohol 2a (526 mg, 82%). 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.27 (s, 1H), 4.34 (m, 1H), 2.62 (s, 1H), 2.24 (s,
3H), 2.00 (s, 3H), 2.06-1.93 (m, 1H), 1.85-1.83 (m, 1H), 1.78-1.74 (m,
1H), 1.20 (s, 3H), 1.12 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 197.5,
158.4, 147.3, 123.7, 118.8, 68.0, 39.1, 32.6, 31.5, 29.0, 27.8, 21.3. IR
(neat) cm-1 3623-3095, 2962, 2930, 2860, 1664, 1603. HRMS (m/z):
calculated for C13H19O2I1Na [M+Na+], 357.0321; found, 357.0322.
