$DATUM 1-(2-Phenylethynylcyclohex-1-enyl)-3-trimethylsilyl-propynol (31b). To a
solution of BuLi (1.8 mL, 2.0 M in hexanes) in THF (3.9 mL) at -78°C was
added trimethylsilylacetylene (0.50 mL, 3.5 mmol) and the resultant
reaction was stirred for 20 min. To this solution was added 30 (0.49 g,
2.3 mmol) in THF (3.9 mL) and the reaction was stirred vigorously. The
reaction was diluted with Et2O, poured into saturated , aqueous NH4Cl and
extracted with Et2O (3x). The combined organic layer was dried over
Na2SO4 and purified with flash chromatography 5% Et2O-petroleum ether to
give 31b as a pale yellow liquid (0.26 g, 85%). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.55 (m, 2H), 7.39 (m, 3H), 5.80 (s, 1H), 2.40 (m, 4H), 2.15 (s, 1H),
1.79 (m, 4H), 0.24 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.9, 131.5,
128.3, 123.3, 118.8, 104.3, 93.4, 90.5, 87.9, 64.6, 30.3, 23.6, 22.2,
22.1, 0.0; IR (NaCl, cm-1) 3155, 3019, 2924, 2852, 2247, 1496, 1452,
1401; HRMS m/z (EI/CI) Expected 308.1596 Found 308.1599.
