$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-[hydroxymethyl-(2-nitrophenyl)]acrylate (1a).
2-Nitrobenzaldehyde (2.00 g, 13.2 mmol) was dissolved in methyl acrylate
(20 mL), DABCO (1.48 g, 13.2 mmol) was added slowly over 5 min upon which
the mixture became a dark orange-red. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 5 days. The methyl acrylate was removed in vacuo, and the
residue was dissolved in Et2O, washed with 1M HCl (3 × 20 mL), and then
with water (2 × 10 mL). The ether extract was concentrated on a rotary
evaporator and then chromatographed over silica gel (Et2O/hexanes, 1:1)
to give 1a as a straw colored oil (3.1 g, 99%), which crystallized from
cold ether. (Rf = 0.28) mp 28-29°C; IR (film) 3445, 2946, 1699, 1537
cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz; d6-acetone) 3.64 (s, 3 H), 5.1 (br s, 1 H), 5.81
(d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.26 (m, 2 H), 7.52 (td, J = 8.1 Hz, 1.8 Hz, 1 H),
7.69 (td, J = 7.8 Hz, J = 1.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.76 (dd, J = 7.8 Hz, 1.8 Hz, 1
H), 7.9 (dd, J = 8.1 Hz, J = 1.2 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (75.45 MHz;
d6-acetone) 51.7, 66.4, 124.4, 124.6, 128.9, 129.2, 133.2, 137.3, 143.1,
148.8, 165.8; MS (EI) 220 (M+-OH, 10), 191 (M+-NO2, 100), 160 (40), 132
(146), 117 (38), 117 (38), 104 (40), 77 (42), 51 (28); HRMS (ESI) calcd
for C11H11NO5Na (M+Na) 260.0535; found: 260.0463.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
