$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 65283-60-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedures: General Procedure for the Reaction
of Furans with n-Butyl glyoxylate (Conditions A, B and C): In a 5 mL
round-bottomed flask closed with a septum, 6,6′-Br2BINOL (conditions A:
18.7 mg, 0.042 mmol; B and C: 46.75 mg, 0.105 mmol) was dissolved in
toluene (A: 0.8 mL; B and C: 2.0 mL). To a stirred solution of the
ligand, titanium tetraisopropoxide (A: 5.9 μL, 5.7 mg, 0.020 mmol, 2.0
mol%; B and C: 14.75 μL, 14.25 mg, 0.050 mmol, 5.0 mol%) was added via
syringe directly under the solution surface at room temperature (inert
atmosphere was not required). The resulting dark red mixture was stirred
for 2 h at room temperature (in conditions A the catalyst solution was
diluted with 3.2 mL of toluene) and cooled to 0°C. Then n-butyl
glyoxylate (0.195 g, 1.5 mmol) was introduced and, finally, after 5-10
min, the corresponding furan (1.0 mmol) was added at 0°C and stirred at
temperature and for time reported in Table 3 (A: 2-3h at 0°C; B: 20h at
20°C; C: 4h at 0°C). The reaction mixture did not require any work-up and
was directly subjected to flash chromatography using hexane followed by
hexane/AcOEt (9:1) as an eluent. The yields of products from substituted
furans (1a, 1c-m) were 76-98% (88-97% ee).
(R)-(5-Ethyl-furan-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (3c): oil 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.26-6.25 (m, 1H), 5.95-5.94 (m, 1H), 5.12 (s, 1H),
4.30-4.17 (m, 2H), 3.27 (s, 1H), 2.65-2.59 (m, 2H), 1.65-1.58 (m, 2H),
1.35-1.26 (m, 2H), 1.21 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3H), 0.89 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H)
ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CHCl3) δ = 171.8 (C), 158.5 (C), 148.9 (C), 109.3
(CH), 104.8 (CH), 66.9 (CH), 66.1 (CH2), 30.4 (CH2), 21.3 (CH2), 18.8
(CH2), 13.5 (CH3), 12.0 (CH3) ppm; IR (CHCl3) 3485, 3130, 3107, 2963,
2937, 2876, 1740, 1559, 1381, 1273, 1210, 1076, 1014, 797 cm-1; HPLC
analysis: 94% ee (OD-H, 5% i-PrOH in hexane, 1.0 mL/min, λ = 205 nm, tR =
6.9 min, minor, tR = 8.8 min, major); [α]D20 = -47.3 (c = 1.7, CHCl3);
HRMS (ESI) calcd. for C12H18O4Na [(M+Na)+]: 249.10973; found: 249.10908.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, ee=94%, Friedel-Crafts reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Enantioselective Synthesis of 2-Furanyl-hydroxyacetates from
Furans via the Friedel-Crafts Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Majer, Jakub; Kwiatkowski, Piotr; Jurczak, Janusz
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(14), 2955-2958

