$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the reaction of 3-bromo-2-silylthiophenes with
aldehydes 3a: Compound 1a (120mg, 0.350mmol) in Et2O (3mL) was cooled to
-78°C. To this solution was added t-BuLi (0.23mL, 1.7M in hexane, 0.38
mmol) dropwise. The resulted mixture was stirred at -78°C for 30 min.
Then, a solution of benzaldehyde (1.05 eq) in Et2O (0.5mL) was added into
the reaction slowly. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C to -20 °C for 60
min and quenched with saturated solution of NH4Cl. The mixture was
extracted with Et2O. Combined organic layers were washed with brine.
After drying with anhydrous Mg2SO4 and evaporation of the solvent, the
residue was purified by flash chromatography to give 3a in 90% yield: 3a,
yield 90%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.09 (d, J = 4.8Hz, 1H), 6.96-6.90
(m, 5H), 6.65 (d, J= 4.8Hz, 1H), 5.69 (s, 1H), 1.74 (s, 1H), 0.03 (s,
9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 151.3, 143.4, 130.3, 128.8, 128.3, 127.3,
126.3, 71.8, 0.7; mass spectrum (ESI) m/z 285.4, [M+Na]+; HRMS m/z
263.0921 [(M+H)+; calcd for C14H19OSSi: 263.0926].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solvent-Controlled Csp2→O Silyl Migration: The "One-Pot" Synthesis of
2,3-Disubstituted Thiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Devarie-Baez, Nelmi O.; Shuhler, Brian J.; Wang, Hua; Xian, Ming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(22), 4655-4658

