$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Reaction of
Thiophenes with n-Butyl Glyoxylate: (In all procedures with BINOL-Ti
catalyst not dried toluene was used and inert atmosphere is not
necessary) Conditions A (for products 9a-9e, 9k): In a 5 mL
round-bottomed flask closed with a septum, 6,6′-Br2BINOL (18.7 mg, 0.042
mmol) was dissolved in 0.8 mL of toluene (not dried). To the stirred
solution of the ligand, titanium tetraisopropoxide (5.9 μL, 5.7 mg, 0.020
mmol, 2.0 mol %) was added via syringe directly under the solution
surface at room temperature (inert atmosphere is not necessary). The
resulting dark red mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature,
diluted with 0.2 mL of toluene, and cooled to -50 °C. n-Butyl glyoxylate
(0.195 g, 1.5 mmol) was introduced and, after 10 min, the corresponding
thiophene (1.0 mmol) was added and stirred for 7 h at -50 °C. The
reaction mixture did not require any work-up and after completion was
directly subjected to flash chromatography using hexane followed by
hexane/AcOEt (9:1) as an eluent. The yields of products obtained from
substituted thiophenes (1a-1e, 1k) were 76-92% (94-98% ee) (see Table 3).
(S)-(5-Methoxy-thiophen-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (9e): oil; 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.71 (dd, J = 3.9 Hz, J = 0.9 Hz, 1H), 6.06 (d,
J = 3.9 Hz, 1H), 5.21 (s, 1H), 4.22 (t, , J = 6.6 Hz, 2H), 3.86 (s, 3H),
3.38 (s, 1H), 1.67-1.59 (m, 2H), 1.38-1.29 (m, 2H), 0.91 (t, J = 7.4 Hz,
3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CHCl3) δ = 172.6 (C), 166.7 (C), 127.0 (C),
123.4 (CH), 103.3 (CH), 69.4 (CH), 66.2 (CH2), 60.2 (CH3), 30.4 (CH2),
18.9 (CH2), 13.6 (CH3) ppm; IR (CHCl3) 3473, 2961, 2938, 2874, 1736,
1560, 1502, 1458, 1431, 1208, 1070, 1044, 996, 774 cm-1; HPLC analysis:
94% ee (AD-H, 5% i-PrOH in hexane, 1.0 mL/min, λ = 256 nm, tR = 17.5 min,
minor, tR = 19.6 min, major); [α]D 20 = -46.9 (c = 1.8, CHCl3); HRMS
(ESI) calcd. for C11H16O4NaS [(M+Na)+]: 267.06615; found: 267.06561.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
