$DATUM TABLE 1, ENTRY 14: (S)-tert-Butyl
2-((S,E)-3-hydroxyhexa-1,5-dien-1-yl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate (29): The
(S,S)-1,3,2-diazaborolidine 4 (R3 = H) was prepared in situ by the
addition of BBr3 (0.38 mL, 1 M in CH2Cl2) into a solution of
(S,S)-1,2-diamino-1,2- diphenylethane bis-N,N-toluenesulfonamide (200 mg,
0.384 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) at 0 °C. This mixture was stirred at 0 °C
for 15 minutes, and then warmed to room temperature and allowed to stir
for 60 minutes. The solvent was removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow
solid was redissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (4 mL) and allowed to stir for 10
minutes. The solvent was again removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow
solid was resuspended in dry CH2Cl2 (4 mL). This sequence was usually
repeated one time prior to the introduction of allyltributylstannane
(0.18 mL, 0.58 mmol), and the mixture was then allowed to stir at room
temperature (8 h). The reaction was then cooled to -78 °C, and a solution
of aldehyde 16 (67.6 mg; 0.30 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was introduced into
the cold solution. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C for 2 hours and was
then quenched at that temperature by the dropwise addition of aqueous pH
7 buffer (2 mL). The quenched reaction mixture was allowed to warm to
room temperature and a solution of saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (7 mL) was
added with additional stirring for 10 min. The phases were separated and
the aqueous phase was extracted three times with CH2Cl2. The combined
organic phases were dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The
resulting residue was washed with hexanes and filtered to remove the
insoluble sulfonamide ligand. The solution of hexanes was concentrated in
vacuo to yield a crude material which was purified by passing the sample
through a column of flash silica gel using EtOAc in hexanes (30:70 by
volume) to give alcohol 29. Analytical HPLC using a silica (2) column and
elution with a gradient of EtOAc in hexanes (10:90 - 30:70 by volume)
showed this material to be a mixture of R/S-diastereomers (6:94 dr).
Preparative HPLC afforded a sample of purified 29 using a standard silica
column with a gradient elution (5% EtOAc in hexanes to 25% EtOAc in
hexanes). Colorless oil, yield 69 mg, 0.258 mmol, 86% (6:94). Rf = 0.18
(30:70 EtOAc to hexanes); [α]D22 -63.4 (c 0.26, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3, 323.1 K) δ (ppm): 5.84 - 5.76 (m, 1H), 5.70 - 5.51 (m, 2H), 5.12
(d, J = 17.5, 1H), 5.10 (d, J = 11.3 Hz, 1H), 4.50 (br s, 1H), 4.20 (m,
1H), 3.43 - 3.36 (m, 1H), 2.38 - 2.25 (m, 2H) 2.12 - 2.05 (m, 1H), 2.00 -
1.77 (m, 1H), 1.71 (s, 3H), 1.66 -1.56 (m, 1H), 1.44 (s, 9H); 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3, 323.1 K) δ (ppm): 154.7, 134.9, 132.3, 117.7, 79.1,
71.4, 58.5, 47.5, 46.6, 40.2, 33.3, 28.8, 24.0; HRMS-ESI (calc. for
C15H25NO3 [M+Na]+) 290.1732, found 290.1740.
