$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Baylis-Hillman
reaction: Enantioselective Baylis-Hillman Reaction Employing 10. To a 10
mL round bottom flask, flame dried and equipped with a stir bar, was
added peptide 10 (0.0015 mmol), dissolved in CHCl3/THF (1:2, 0.5M),
L-proline (0.0015 mmol), aldehyde 1 (0.015 mmol), and methyl vinyl ketone
(0.029 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred until complete loss of
starting material was observed by TLC (2:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate). The
reaction was diluted with chloroform and purification via flash
chromatography (SiO2, CHCl3). 2.7 mg (81%) of 2 as a pale yellow oil.
3-[(2,4-Dinitro-phenyl)-hydroxy-methyl]-but-3-en-2-one (25). 1 H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.80 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 8.48 (dd, J = 8.4, 2.2 Hz,
1H), 8.05 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.30 (s, 1H), 6.23 (s, 1H), 5.85 (s, 1H),
3.55 (bs, 1H), 2.38 (s, 3H); 13 C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 199.5, 148.1,
147.9, 147.2, 143.2, 130.6, 127.3, 127.1, 120.1, 67.4, 25.9; IR (film,
cm-1) 3408, 3106, 2357, 1673, 1606, 1536, 1347; TLC R f 0.43 (40% ethyl
acetate/hexanes); [α]D -135 (1.0, CHCl3, 63% ee); Exact mass calcd for
[C11H10N2O6 + Na]+ requires m/z 289.0437. Found 289.0430 (ESI+). Assay of
enantiomeric purity: Enantiomers of product were separated by chiral HPLC
employing a Chiralcel OJ column (Diacel). Conditions: 90:10
hexanes:ethanol; Flow rate 0.75 mL/min; 54.3 min (major ent), 63.1 min
(minor ent).
