$DATUM 18g. To a solution of the (S,S) Duthaler-Hafner titanium complex (5.42 g,
8.85 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in Et2O (111 mL) at 0 °C was added dropwise
allylmagnesium chloride (2.0 M in THF, 3.8 mL, 1.3 equiv) over 5 min and
the mixture was maintained for 1.5 h. The mixture was then cooled to –78
°C. To the mixture was added dropwise a solution ofaldehyde 18f (3.08 g,
5.90 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in Et2O (30 mL) over 10 min and the mixture was
maintained for 4 h. The reaction was quenched with water and was allowed
to warm to ambient temperature and was stirred vigorously for 16 h. The
mixture was filtered through celite® and the layers were separated. The
organic phase was washed twice with water and once with brine. The
combined aqueous layers were extracted twice with EtOAc. The combined
organic phases were dried with MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (15–30% EtOAc/hexanes)
furnished 3.20 g (96%) of homoallylic alcohol 18g as a pale yellow oil:
[α]22 D +8.5 (c 1.19, CH3Cl); IR (neat) 3462, 3072, 2932, 1739, 1428,
1240, 1113; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.67–7.64 (m, 4H), 7.45–7.37 (m,
6H), 5.79 (dt, J = 17.1, 10.3, 7.0, 1H), 5.66– 5.61 (m, 1H), 5.58–5.54
(m, 2H), 5.49 (dd, J = 15.5, 6.8, 1H), 5.22 (q, J = 6.5, 1H), 5.15– 5.11
(m, 2H), 5.02–4.99 (m, 1H), 4.12–4.10 (m, 1H), 3.70–3.65 (m, 2H),
2.47–2.42 (m, 1H), 2.37–2.23 (m, 5H), 2.02 (s, 3H), 2.01 (s, 3H), 1.75
(s, br, 1H), 1.05 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.8, 170.4,
135.9, 135.81, 135.75, 134.4, 133.54, 133.50, 131.3, 129.98, 129.96,
128.9, 127.93, 127.92, 126.0, 118.3, 73.7, 73.6, 71.6, 64.7, 42.1, 37.4,
33.8, 26.9, 21.4, 21.3, 19.5; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C33H44O6SiNa [M +
Na]+ 587.2805, found 587.2813.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
