$DATUM 2.2. 1-(2,3-Diallyloxy-phenyl)-ethanolTo 2,3-bis-allyloxybenzaldehyde
(11) (1.0 g, 4.5 mmol) in THF (10 ml) was added dropwise methylmagnesium
bromide (1.5 mL, 4.5 mmol) in DCM (1.5 mL) over 15 min at 0 °C. The
mixture was stirred for 4 h, and at r.t for 1 h. The reaction mixture was
quenched with 10% acetic acid solution (25 mL) and ice, and extracted in
EtOAc (3 × 50 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with aqueous
sodium metabisulfite solution (2 × 50 mL), dried (MgSO4) and solvent was
removed. Theresidue was purified by chromatography on silica with
EtOAc/petroleum ether (15:85, v/v) as eluent, to give the product as
colourless oil (0.88 g, 82%). 2.2. 1-(2,3-Diallyloxy-phenyl)-ethanol,
Yield (0.88 g, 82%). 1H-NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.40 (3H, d, J = 6.5Hz),
4.5-4.4 (4H, m), 5.10 (1H, q, J = 6.5 Hz), 5.3-5.4 (4H, m), 5.9-6.0 (2H,
m), 6.6-6.8 (1H, m), 7.00 (2H, m). 13C NMR (75MHz. CDCl3): δ 24.1, 66.3,
69.9, 74.3, 117.8, 118.1, 118.6, 124.5, 130.0, 133.5, 134.5, 139.7,
145.5, 151.7. IR: 2992, 2922, 1584, 1471, 1265, 1197, 985, 921, 786cm-1.
HRMS: [M+NH4] + calc. 252.1594, found 252.1598.
