$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedures: A. 1-(2-Allyloxyphenyl)-2,2,2-trichloroethanol 1l: To
a mixture of 2-allyloxybenzaldehyde (1.62 g, 0.01 mol) and chloroform
(2.38 g, 0.02 mol) was added DBU (1.52 g, 0.01 mol) drop wise under a
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at ambient
temperature and then diluted with chloroform (50 mL) and washed with 2 N
HCl (15 x 5mL). The chloroform layer was dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography (silica gel, 5% ethyl acetate in hexane).
1-(2-Allyloxyphenyl)-2,2,2-trichloroethanol as colorless liquid, yield
2.2 g, 79%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.10-4.18 (m, broad,
D2O-exchangeable, 1H), 4.61 (d, J = 5.1 Hz, 2H), 5.31 (dd, J = 10.5, 1.2
Hz, 1H), 5.43 (dd, J = 17.1, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.65 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H),
6.00-6.12 (m, 1H), 6.93 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.02 (dt, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H),
7.35 (t, J = 8.6, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.62 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.4 Hz, 1H) ppm; 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 69.3 (CH2), 80.4 (CH), 103.5 (C), 112.2 (CH),
118.0 (CH2), 120.6 (CH), 123.5 (C), 130.45 (CH), 130.49 (CH), 132.6 (CH),
156.7 (C) ppm; IR (neat): 3446(s), 3079(w), 2926(m), 2864(m), 1596(s),
1492(s), 1454(s), 1292(s), 1244 (s), 1119(m), 1057(s), 995 (s), 930(s),
822(s), 76 (s) cm-1 . HRMS (M + Na+): calc for C11H11O2Cl3Na: 302.9722,
found: 302.9724.
