$DATUM Conditions B (for products 9f, 9g): In a 5 mL round-bottomed flask closed
with a septum, 6,6′-Br2BINOL (46.75 mg, 0.105 mmol) was dissolved in 2.0
mL of toluene. To the stirred solution of the ligand, titanium
tetraisopropoxide (14.75 μL, 14.25 mg, 0.050 mmol, 5.0 mol%) was added
via syringe directly under the solution surface at room temperature. The
resulting dark red mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature. Solid
thiophene (1f or 1g, 1.0 mmol) was introduced and stirred for 10 min at
20 °C (in case of 1f the mixture was diluted with 1.0 mL of toluene to
improve solubility). The mixture was cooled to 0 °C and n-butyl
glyoxylate (0.195 g, 1.5 mmol) was added and stirred at 0 °C for 4 h. The
reaction mixture did not require any work-up and was directly subjected
to flash chromatography using hexane followed by hexane/AcOEt (9:1) as an
eluent. The yields of product obtained from 1f and 1g were 97% (94% ee)
and 85% (94% ee) respectively (see Table 3).
(S)-(5-Styryl-furan-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (9f): m.p.:
77.0-78.5°C (crystallised from AcOEt/hexane); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ =
7.46-7.43 (m, 2H), 7.36-7.32 (m, 2H), 7.26-7.23 (m, 1H), 7.15 (d, J =
16.1 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (dm, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 6.93 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 6.88
(d, J = 16.1 Hz, 1H), 5.35 (s, 1H), 4.29-4.19 (m, 2H), 3.53 (s, 1H),
1.68-1.61 (m, 2H), 1.39-1.30 (m, 2H), 0.91 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CHCl3) δ = 172.4 (C), 143.2 (C), 140.1 (C), 136.8 (C),
128.7 (CH), 128.6 (CH), 127.7 (CH), 126.3 (CH), 125.9 (CH), 121.6 (CH),
69.2 (CH), 66.5 (CH2), 30.4 (CH2), 18.9 (CH2), 13.6 (CH3) ppm; IR (CHCl3)
3437, 3023, 2958, 2931, 2871, 1728, 1625, 1596, 1495, 1446, 1205, 1086,
953, 797, 772, 754, 691 cm-1; HPLC analysis: 94% ee (OD-H, 5% i-PrOH in
hexane, 1.0 mL/min, λ = 225 nm, tR = 14.1 min, minor, tR = 19.5 min,
major); [α]D 20 = +27.0 (c = 2.2, CHCl3); HRMS (ESI) calcd. for
C18H20O3NaS [(M+Na)+]: 339.10254; found: 339.10229.
