$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for reaction of
(E)-1-bromovinyl lithium reagent with electrophiles:
1,1-Dibromo-3,3,3-trifluoro-2-[(methoxymethoxy)methyl]prop-1-ene (164 mg,
0.5 mmol) dissolved in THF (5 mL) and the mixture was cooled to -78°C.
Butyl lithium (2 mol/L in cyclohexane, 0.25 mL, 0.5 mmol) was added
slowly to the mixture and stirred for 0.5 h. Iodine (254 mg, 1mmol) was
added and stirred for another 1 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with
water and extracted with ether (30 mL×3). The organic phase was washed
with water (30 mL×3), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Removing the solvent
and subsequent column chromatography gave
(Z)-1-bromo-3,3,3-trifluoro-1-iodo-2-[(methoxymethoxy)methyl]prop-1-ene
(177 mg, 95%) as a colorless liquid.
(E)-2-bromo-4,4,4-trifluoro-1-(4-fluorophenyl)-3-[(methoxymethoxy)methyl]but-2-en-1-ol,
yield: 75%, white solid, m. p.: 52-53°C; νmax (neat) /cm-1 3387, 2968,
2901, 1631, 1510, 1314, 1123, 1024, 997, 904, 838, 606; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.42-7.37 (m, 2H), 7.10-7.04 (m, 2H), 5.95 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H),
4.69 (s, 2H), 4.49 (s, 2H), 3.41 (s, 3H), 2.71 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H); 19F
NMR (282 MHz) δ -55.88 (s, 3F), -114.30 (m, 1F); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz) δ
162.56 (d, J = 247.0 Hz), 164.81 (d, J = 2.5 Hz), 134.70 (d, J = 2.1 Hz),
129.16 (q, J = 29.6 Hz), 127.64 (d, J = 8.2 Hz), 122.73 (q, J = 277.6
Hz), 115.38 (d, J = 21.7 Hz), 96.31, 71.48 (d, J = 1.6 Hz), 66.53, 55.65;
MS (EI) m/z 372 (M+. , 1.1), 45 (100); Anal. Calcd for C13H13BrF4O3: C,
41.85; H, 3.51; Found: C, 41.90; H, 3.52.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
