$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 20 (425 mg, 2.0 mmol) in toluene (1.0 mL) was added
2-bromo-1-cyclohexenecarbaldehyde 4S1 (378 mg, 2.0 mmol), triethylamine
(0.56 mL, 4.0 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (55 mg, 0.060 mmol), PPh3 (93 mg, 0.36
mmol), CuI (34 mg, 0.18 mmol) at 0 °C and the mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 24 h under dark. The reaction mixture was quenched with
saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution and the aqueous layer was extracted with
Et2O (10 mL×3). The combined organic layer was washed with water and
dried over MgSO4. The organic solvent was removed under reduced pressure
and the residue was subjected to flash column chromatography on silica
gel with hexane/AcOEt (v/v = 10/1) as eluents to afford the corresponding
coupling product 21 Brown oil, (641 mg, 2.0 mmol, quant). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.56-1.67 (m, 8H), 2.24-2.28 (m, 6H), 2.42-2.45 (m, 2H),
6.05 (s, 1H), 7.26-7.42 (m, 5H), 10.2 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd- and Cu-Catalyzed One-Pot Multicomponent Synthesis of Hetero
α,α'-Dimers of Heterocycles
