$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: A glass vial equipped with
a magnetic stirrer bar was charged with the aldehyde 1 (0.1 mmol, 1
equiv), the aminocatalyst 2 (0.005 mmol, 0.05 equiv) and toluene (0.2
mL). After short stirring at rt, H2O2 (35 wt% in water, 0.105 mmol, 1.05
equiv) was added. The stirring was maintained at ambient temperature for
24 h to achieve full conversion of the aldehyde 1. Upon completion of the
reaction, MgSO4 (0.25 mmol, 2.5 equiv) was added, followed by thioamide 5
(0.12 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and Cs2CO3 (0.2 mmol, 2 equiv). The mixture was
left stirring for 2 h, and then loaded directly on silica gel in a
column. After waiting for 10 min, FC afforded the thiophene 9. Notably,
the formed products are sensitive to CHCl3. 9e (R,E)-Methyl
2-(dimethylamino)-5-(1-hydroxyhept-4-enyl)thiophene-3-carboxylate (Entry
5, Table 2) Following the general procedure 9e was isolated by FC
(gradient: EtOAc/pentane 15:85 to EtOAc/pentane 25:75) in 73% yield as a
pale yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ 7.03 (s, 1H), 5.52-5.35 (m,
2H), 4.63 (t, J= 6.8 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 2.96 (s, 6H), 2.12-1.93 (m,
4H), 1.88-1.68 (m, 2H), 0.97 (t, J= 7.5 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CD3OD)
δ ppm 168.4, 165.0, 134.7, 133.8, 129.3, 126.0, 111.6, 70.5, 51.6, 46.0
(2C), 39.5, 29.8, 26.6, 14.4. HR-MS: calculated for (M+Na): 320.1297;
found: 320.1291. The ee was determined by HPLC using a Chiralpak IC
column (hexane/iPrOH 90:10, 1 mL min-1); τmajor = 17.5 min, τminor = 23.7
min (96% ee). [α]D rt: -27.5 (c = 1.01, MeOH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (96% ee), product was sensitive to CHCl3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Optically active thiophenes via an organocatalytic one-pot methodology
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ransborg, Lars Krogager; Albrecht, Lukasz; Weise, Christian F.; Bak,
Jesper R.; Joergensen, Karl Anker
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(3), 724-727

