$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM TABLE 1, ENTRY 6:
(4R,7S,E)-7-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-4-hydroxy-5-methyl-2-methyleneoct-5-en-1-yl
benzoate (21): The asymmetric allylation began with formation of the
(R,R)-reagent 5 (R3 = CH2OBz) by the addition of BBr3 (0.20 mL, 1 M in
CH2Cl2) into a solution of (R,R)-1,2-diamino-1,2-diphenylethane
bis-N,N-toluenesulfonamide (104.2 mg, 0.20 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.3 mL) at 0
°C. This mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 15 minutes, and then warmed to
room temperature and allowed to stir for 60 minutes. The solvent was
removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was redissolved in dry
CH2Cl2 (2 mL) and allowed to stir for 10 minutes. The solvent was again
removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was resuspended in dry
CH2Cl2 (2 mL). This sequence was usually repeated one more time prior to
the introduction of 2-[(tri-n-butylstannyl)methyl]-2-propen-1-ol benzoate
(132 mg, 0.28 mmol), and the mixture was then allowed to stir at room
temperature overnight (8-9 hrs). The reaction was then cooled to - 78 °C,
and a solution of aldehyde 12 (53 mg; 0.15 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was
introduced into the cold solution. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C for
2 hours and was then quenched at that temperature by the dropwise
addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer (1 mL). The quenched reaction mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature and a solution of saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added with additional stirring for 10 min. The phases
were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted three times with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was washed with hexanes and
filtered to remove the insoluble sulfonamide ligand. The solution of
hexanes was concentrated in vacuo to yield a crude material which was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc in hexanes)
affording alcohol 21. This sample was shown to be a mixture of two
diastereomers (95:5 dr) by HPLC. Purification of 21 by preparative HPLC
on a standard silica gel column using gradient elution (EtOAc in hexanes
0:100 - 14:86 by volume) gave a sample for characterization. Yield 59.5
mg, 0.113 mmol, 75% (95:5). Rf = 0.43 (80:20 hexanes:EtOAc by volume);
[α]D22 -26.3 (c 0.10, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 8.07 (dd,
J = 8.3, 0.98 Hz, 2H), 7.67 - 7.63 (m, 4H), 7.63 - 7.56 (m, 1H), 7.46 -
7.30 (m, 8H), 5.49 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (q, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.07
(d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.79 (ABq, JAB = 13.6 Hz, 2H), 4.57 - 4.52 (m, 1H),
4.05 (ap t, J = 6.1 Hz, 1H), 2.20 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 1.23 (d, J = 0.90
Hz, 3H), 1.20 (d, J = 5.8 Hz, 3H), 1.02 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3)
δ (ppm): 166.22, 140.88, 135.84, 135.78, 135.42, 134.61, 134.42, 134.36,
133.08, 131.09, 129.63, 129.50, 129.44, 128.43, 127.50, 127.35, 115.24,
74.91, 67.06, 66.44, 39.54, 26.92, 24.18, 19.12, 11.82; HRMS-ESI (calc.
for C33H40O4Si [M+Na]+) 551.2594, found 551.2583.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, agent dependent stereochemistry, in-situ generated
reactant in stage 2, buffered solution used in stage 4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereocontrol in Asymmetric SE' Reactions of γ-Substituted
α,β-Unsaturated Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Williams, David R.; Atwater, Bruce A.; Bawel, Seth A.; Ke, Pucheng;
Gutierrez, Osvaldo; Tantillo, Dean J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(2), 468-471

