$DATUM (±)-1-(3',4'-Diacetoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (1g). A stirred solution of
3,4-diacetoxybenzaldehyde (1 g, 4.5 mmol) and allyl iodide (0.41 mL, 4.5
mmol) in water (100 mL) was treated with indium powder (0.52g, 4.5 mmol).
The solution was stirred vigorously for 48 h and then extracted with
ethyl acetate (3 x 100 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed
with water (2 x 50 mL) and brine (50 mL), and dried (MgSO4). The solvent
was evaporated under reduced pressure to yield the crude product which
was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel eluting with ethyl
acetate in hexane to yield alcohol 1g as a pale yellow oil (1.09 g, 92%):
(±)-1-(3',4'-Diacetoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (1g), yield 1.09 g, 92% silica
gel TLC Rf 0.36 (50% ethyl acetate-hexane); 1H NMR (270 MHz) δ 2.28 (s,
6H), 2.36-2.58 (m, 2H), 4.73 (dd, J= 7.9, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 5.13-5.16 (m, 1H),
5.17-5.22 (m, 1H), 5.72-5.89 (m, 1H), 7.14-7.27 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (68 MHz)
δ 20.6 (two carbons), 43.7, 72.4, 118.7, 120.9, 123.3, 123.9, 134.1,
141.3, 142.1, 143.0, 168.2, 168.3; FT-IR (neat) 3462, 1773, 1641, 1603
cm-1 ; MS (EI) m/z 264 (M% 0.2), 247 (2), 223 (58), 181 (78), 139 (100),
93 (32). HRMS (EI) calcd for C14H16O5 (M) 264.0998, found (M+) 264.0998.
