$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-1-(3',4'-Diacetoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (18).1 A stirred solution of
[(-)-B-chlorodiisopinocampheyl borane] (2.17 g, 6.25 mmol) in dry THF (25
ml) was cooled to -78°C and treated with allyl magnesium chloride (338
ml, 6.75 mmol, 2.0 M in THF) under nitrogen. The solution was stirred for
I h and allowed to warm to rt over a further 1 h. The solution was cooled
to -78°C and treated with a solution of aldehyde (1 g, 4.5 mmol) in dry
THF (10 ml). The solution was stirred for 1 h and allowed to warm to rt
over a 1 h. The solution was treated with a pre-formed mixture of 3.0 M
sodium hydroxide (3.29 ml, 9.9 mmol) and 30% hydrogen peroxide (1.37 ml,
11.25 mmol). After 10 min the mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (i50
mi), washed with water (2 x 50 ml) and brine (50 ml) and dried (MgSO4).
The solvent evaporated under reduced pressure to yield the crude product
which was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel eluting with an
increasing proportion of ethyl acetate in petrol from 0 to 40% to yield
alcohol 18 (892 mg, 75%, 90% ee) as a pale yellow oil:
(S)-1-(3',4'-Diacetoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (18), Yield 892 mg, 75%
(Found: C, 63.3; H, 6.2. C14H16O5 requires C, 63.6; H, 6.1%); silica gel
TLC Rf 0.36 (50% ethyl acetate-petrol); [α]20 D -32.1 (c 1.2, CHCl3);
Spectral data as previously reported for racemic compound.2
