Morita-Baylis-Hillman reaction co-catalysed by a thiourea for the
synthesis of multifunctional 2-hydroxy-3-nitro-4-arylbut-3-enoate
derivatives (a-i) via the reaction of various nitroalkenes with ethyl
glyoxylate in the presence of DMAP or imidazole according to in the
following Scheme (See: Kuan, H.-H.; Reddy, R. J.; Chen, K. Tetrahedron
2010, 66, 9875). c
