$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure 8. Vinylogous Aldol
Additions of Conjugated N,O-Silyl Ketene Acetals to Conjugated Aldehydes.
Preparation of (+)-4-[(5R,2E)-1-Oxo-5-phenyl-5-hydroxy-2-pentenyl]
morpholine (50) (Table 8, entry 1). Diisopropylethylamine (18 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv) was added via syringe to a flamedried, 20-mL, Schlenk
flask under Ar containing a solution of 42 mg (0.05 mmol, 0.05 equiv) of
bisphosphoramide (R,R)-3 in CH2Cl2 (5 mL). To this solution was added 102
μL (1.0 mmol) of benzaldehyde in one portion. To the resulting solution
was added 126 μL (1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv) of SiCl4 in one portion, and the
reaction mixture was cooled to -72 °C over 15 min. Then, a solution of
324 mg (1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) of 45 in 5 mL of CH2Cl2 was added dropwise
over 5 min via syringe. The resulting mixture was stirred at -72 °C for 1
h whereupon 3.0 mL of chilled CH2- Cl2 was added before the cold reaction
mixture was poured into a rapidly stirring solution of 1:1 satd aq
NaHCO3/satd aq KF (25 mL) at 0 °C. This biphasic mixture was stirred
vigorously for 3 h after which the organic layer was removed and aqueous
layer was washed with CH2Cl2 (3 × 50 mL). The combined organic extracts
were dried over Na2SO4 (5 g) and filtered, and the filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo. The ratio of γ:α-addition products was determined
to be >99:1 by 1H NMR (500 MHz) analysis of the crude reaction mixture.
The residue was purified by column chromatography (SiO2 (30 g), 3 cm
diameter, EtOAc (200 mL) to EtOAc/MeOH, 19:1 (150 mL)) to yield a solid
which was recrystallized by precipitation from hot EtOAc (5 mL) with
minimal amounts of hexanes to yield 247 mg (95%) of (+)-50 as white
needles. Preparation of
(+)-4-[(5R,2E)-1-Oxo-7-phenyl-6-methyl-5-hydroxy-2,6-heptadienyl]morpholine
(55) (Table 8, entry 6) Following Representative Procedure 8, 140 µL (1.0
mmol) of α-methylcinnamaldehyde was combined with 42 mg (0.05 mmol, 0.05
equiv) of bisphosphoramide (R,R)-3, 18 µL (0.1 mmol, 0.1 equiv) of
diisopropylethylamine, 126 µL (1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv) of SiCl4 and 324 mg
(1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) of 45 to yield, after column chromatography (SiO2
(30 g), 3 cm diam., EtOAc (200 mL) to EtOAc/MeOH, 19/1 (150 mL)) an oil
which was crystallized from Et2O (4 mL) to yield 273 mg (91%) of (+)-55
as white crystals. The ratio of γ/α-addition products was determined to
be >99/1 by 1H NMR (500 MHz) analysis of the crude reaction mixture. Data
for (+)-55: mp: 79-80 °C (Et2O) 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.37 (dt, J =
7.6, 1.3, 2 H, HC(10)), 7.27 (dt, J = 7.6, 1.7, 2 H, HC(9)) 7.25 (dt, J =
7.5, 1.2, 1 H, HC(11)), 6.91 (dt, J = 15.0, 7.3, 1 H, HC(3)), 6.54 (s, 1
H, HC(7)), 6.32 (dt, J = 15.1, 1.3, 1 H, HC(2)), 4.34 (t, J = 6.6, 1 H,
HC(5)), 3.66-3.61 (m, 8 H, H2C(12,13)), 2.59-2.55 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 2.01
(br s, 1 H, OH), 1.90 (d, J = 1.2, 3 H, H3C(14)) 13C NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3
165.5 (C(1)), 142.8 (C(3)), 139.3 (C(6)), 137.2 (C(8)), 128.8 (C(9)),
128.0 (C(10)), 126.4 (C(11)), 125.7 (C(7)), 122.4 (C(2)), 76.1 (C(5)),
66.48 (C(13)), 66.54 (C(13), 46.0 (C(12)), 45.1 (C(12)), 38.6 (C(4)),
13.5 (C(14)) IR: (neat) 3392 (m), 3055 (m), 3023 (w), 2966 (m), 2918 (m),
2858 (m), 2714 (w), 2361 (w), 2243 (w), 1957 (w), 1812 (w), 1659 (s),
1606 (s), 1491 (m), 1436 (s), 1362 (m), 1301 (m), 1267 (s), 1236 (s),
1190 (m), 1116 (s), 1069 (m), 1042 (s), 1019 (m), 977 (m), 920 (m), 855
(m), 810 (w), 733 (s), 701 (s), 646 (m), 619 (w) MS: (EI, 70 eV) 301 (M+,
2), 155 (66), 147 (40), 140 (30), 129 (24), 115 (10), 91 (18), 87 (11),
69 (14), 62 (100), 61 (26) Opt. Rot.: [α]D 24 +0.82 (c = 1.07, EtOH) TLC:
Rf 0.14 (EtOAc) [UV(254 nm)] SFC: (R)-55, t R 8.67 min (75.5 %); (S)- 55,
t R 10.02 min (24.5 %) (Chiralpak OB, 150 psi, 40 ºC, 5.0% MeOH in CO2,
3.5 mL/min, 220 nm) Analysis: C18H23NO3 (301.38) Calcd: C, 71.73; H,
7.69; N, 4.65% Found: C, 71.68; H, 7.73; N, 4.66%
